1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,620
It'll be impossible for us to eat all this.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,060
Oh, there you are.

3
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,440
Why do you look like that?

4
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:49,340
I thought I gave you a mission to search for His Majesty.

5
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:53,680
I do not recall allowing you to rest.

6
00:00:53,680 --> 00:01:00,660
What the hell was that?

7
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:03,920
My sword just fell from against the wall.

8
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:06,720
Tie that stupid thing up already.

9
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:09,540
Fallon?

10
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:12,560
Marcel. Marcel!

11
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:15,620
Where's Fallon?

12
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,680
Uh, what?

13
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:21,060
Hey, have you seen Fallon anywhere?

14
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,980
Can't say anyone's passed by.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,520
What? Did something happen?

16
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,040
It can't be.

17
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:31,900
Did she leave from this window?

18
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:36,740
I'm gonna look outside.

19
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,200
Huh?

20
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,680
Why is it...

21
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,300
Fallon!

22
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:54,460
Hey, what's wrong?

23
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:56,520
Are you...

24
00:01:56,520 --> 00:02:01,320
Are you okay? Tell me what happened.

25
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,420
I must find him.

26
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,140
I must find Lord Delgall.

27
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:07,460
Wait a sec.

28
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:08,800
How...

29
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,020
In this kingdom...

30
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,020
Everything that you can see...

31
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:14,020
Buildings...

32
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:15,020
Currency...

33
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:16,020
Livestock...

34
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:17,020
Citizens...

35
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:18,020
Blood...

36
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:19,020
And meat.

37
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:24,660
Even each and every tiny grain of sand that you crush beneath your feet.

38
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:29,220
All of it is the personal property of his majesty, King Delgall.

39
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:30,820
And only his.

40
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,680
Do you understand, you disgusting thief?

41
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:37,520
You.

42
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,100
I remember you.

43
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:42,240
You were wandering around in the paintings.

44
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:43,900
The paintings?

45
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,580
That's right.

46
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,420
But who is he?

47
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:49,780
You vile intruder.

48
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:51,960
Just what is it that you want?

49
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,680
It's the Lord of the Dungeon.

50
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,380
The Mad Mage himself.

51
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:05,140
You.

52
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,540
You get away from them.

53
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:07,600
Do you hear me?

54
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:09,280
I won't miss again.

55
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:14,720
You should know your place, you filth.

56
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:17,100
Hey, let's go.

57
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:17,980
Come on.

58
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:20,940
Shut up!

59
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:26,040
L-Laios!

60
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,240
Such amazing strength.

61
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,700
What the hell is going on here?

62
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:32,300
Is he an adventurer?

63
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:36,300
Spellbook?

64
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,700
I have a bad feeling about this.

65
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:44,040
Is that some kind of magic chant?

66
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,480
This chanting could only be...

67
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:55,240
Ancient magic!

68
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,020
To bury them all!

69
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:07,100
Explosion magic.

70
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:08,240
Abjuration magic.

71
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,920
No, those won't work.

72
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:11,240
Then...

73
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:20,340
I'll overwrite the spell instead.

74
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,080
Dispel!

75
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:35,660
Dispel!

76
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:40,160
This ancient magic?

77
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,940
I can understand it.

78
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:43,020
I can read it.

79
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:43,660
But...

80
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:49,460
I can't keep up with it!

81
00:04:49,460 --> 00:05:12,980
Are you the one who made this dungeon?

82
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:13,980
I need...

83
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,560
I need...

84
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,980
To talk to you about...

85
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:17,800
I...

86
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:38,700
Don't look so worried.

87
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,640
The thieves are gone now.

88
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:45,360
And his majesty will soon be returning.

89
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,060
When he does, we'll be sure to celebrate.

90
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:51,400
Hey, dragon.

91
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:56,340
That must be inconvenient.

92
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:59,400
Let me change your form for you.

93
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:10,520
Do what you have been ordered to.

94
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:13,400
Yes.

95
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:19,780
What happened?

96
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:21,140
Hold on.

97
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,200
I'll get lights up.

98
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:27,760
What is this place?

99
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:30,180
Come to think of it, where did we fall from?

100
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:31,920
How do we leave?

101
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:33,380
There's no...

102
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:35,880
What's happening?

103
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:36,840
Oh, no.

104
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:38,540
Are the walls closing in?

105
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:40,120
You've got to be kidding me!

106
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:40,880
Dammit!

107
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:42,200
We've got to look for an exit!

108
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:42,860
Where?

109
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:45,280
Can't you fix it with magic or something?

110
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,260
And what kind of magic do you suggest?

111
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:56,700
We're dead.

112
00:06:57,400 --> 00:07:01,780
This won't be my first time dying, but no one is going to find us under rocks.

113
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,540
We just got Fallon back.

114
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:07,240
And I was so close to the dungeon's secrets.

115
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:09,240
It'll have been for nothing.

116
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,700
It can't end like this.

117
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:18,280
Marcel, no!

118
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:21,240
Whoa, it's a tunnel!

119
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:22,720
Let's use it to get out!

120
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:25,400
What, we don't even know where it ends up?

121
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:27,800
It's better than becoming a pancake!

122
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,220
Just hurry up and go!

123
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:40,700
Where the hell are we?

124
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:46,340
Wherever it is, we've got to get out and fast.

125
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:51,160
I... I can't even move a finger right now.

126
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,780
You've got to get up!

127
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:55,340
If that guy finds us again, we're...

128
00:07:55,340 --> 00:08:04,840
It's... it's over.

129
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:05,840
It's over.

130
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,980
It's over.

131
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,380
There's no need to...

132
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:19,300
They... they disappeared?

133
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:21,040
Ugh, damn it.

134
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:22,820
I think I'm going crazy.

135
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:27,620
Senshi, I need you to wake up Lyos for me.

136
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:30,080
I'm gonna go look around a little bit.

137
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:37,160
Get him!

138
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:39,080
How did he manage to sneak in here?

139
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,000
The long ears with them!

140
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:42,140
There he is!

141
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:43,100
Come here, you!

142
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:44,740
Quiet down!

143
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,680
What's going on?

144
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:48,440
We found some moles, Captain.

145
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:49,800
How'd they get in here?

146
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:51,800
Why'd the watch not catch them?

147
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,380
To be honest, we don't know.

148
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,320
The hole's closed up now.

149
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:56,960
Whatever.

150
00:08:56,960 --> 00:09:05,200
A tiny man, an underground dweller, a long legs, and a long ear.

151
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,440
How perfect!

152
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:10,640
I've never killed a long ear before, but now I can.

153
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:12,840
Give the small one to the dogs.

154
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:14,740
They're starved for entertainment.

155
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:16,060
Wait.

156
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:19,780
You wouldn't happen to be Chief Zone's younger sister, would you, Miss?

157
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:24,400
The reason we came here was actually to fulfill a promise with the Chief.

158
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:26,480
So mind showing us mercy?

159
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:29,860
How do you know that name?

160
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:35,960
Hold on.

161
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:36,820
We know you.

162
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:39,320
You're since way different, vegetable seller.

163
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:42,760
It must have been important for you to come this far.

164
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:45,320
What was the promise you made with him?

165
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:48,420
I see.

166
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:51,100
Things are making a lot more sense now.

167
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:55,180
I did think it was weird that the dragon didn't seem to be around anymore.

168
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:58,400
In place of my brother, I thank you.

169
00:09:59,060 --> 00:10:00,080
Go prepare the medicine!

170
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:09,880
It's ready.

171
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:09,940
It's ready.

172
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:49,220
Oh, hey.

173
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:52,540
We were attacked by a magic-using elf earlier.

174
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:54,580
You know anything?

175
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:55,820
Like, maybe...

176
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:57,120
What did the elf look like?

177
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,780
Oh, uh, he had brown skin?

178
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:00,840
And silver hair?

179
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:01,600
That's him.

180
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:04,280
I can't say I know many details.

181
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:08,440
What I do know is, he was here long before we were.

182
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:10,420
And seems to rule over the dungeon.

183
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:15,100
If someone from the outside starts to meddle with the dungeon more than necessary,

184
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:16,980
then he appears.

185
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:20,200
He creates monsters and controls them.

186
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:21,660
Changes the terrain.

187
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:25,200
And can kill anything simply by opening that buck.

188
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:28,140
Wait, he rules over the dungeon?

189
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:31,640
So then, that was the mad mage?

190
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,960
We've caught the attention of the mad mage?

191
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,520
You've gotta be kidding.

192
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:37,960
Dammit, we need to get out of here now!

193
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,460
Did Marcel's magic call him to us?

194
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,040
Or is it because we killed the dragon?

195
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:47,180
He has several monsters working under him.

196
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:50,380
If you killed one of them, then you probably made him angry.

197
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:56,780
To protect us from that fate, my brother made sure to tell us never to touch the red dragon.

198
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:59,420
Brother's right about everything.

199
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:00,700
That bastard!

200
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:04,960
When they wake up, they'll definitely want to start looking for Fallon.

201
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,560
I need to make them give up no matter the cost.

202
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:09,680
What'll you do?

203
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,660
Whatever it takes.

204
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,100
Burn the staff to ashes.

205
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:15,080
Say we saw Fallon head for the surface.

206
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:18,460
Or tell them she was satisfied after eating the dragon meat.

207
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:21,160
So you plan to lie to him?

208
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,040
Of course I do!

209
00:12:23,340 --> 00:12:26,200
If I don't lie, then those two idiots are never gonna give up!

210
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:29,500
If we go any further, then we're definitely gonna get killed.

211
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,880
Do you want to become part of the wall?

212
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:33,180
Cause I sure don't!

213
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:34,460
I...

214
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:42,840
There's absolutely no way I'm dying with those two.

215
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:46,000
Hey, uh...

216
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,200
I'd like to go grab what we left behind.

217
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:50,340
Would you mind taking me there?

218
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:54,620
Yes, I mind.

219
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:57,860
The stench of your cowardly nature might rub off on me.

220
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:58,520
What?

221
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,920
I'm asking you to...

222
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,320
Can you please take him back?

223
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:06,120
He is a coward, but he's not a bad person.

224
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:07,360
Senshi!

225
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:08,920
You're not coming along?

226
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:12,380
Someone needs to stay by Laios and Marcil's side.

227
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:13,300
What?

228
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:20,200
If it's coming from you, I can't argue.

229
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,240
I hate it, but fine.

230
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:23,240
I'll guide him there.

231
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:31,500
Damn it.

232
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:35,360
I can't believe I'm surrounded by such idiots!

233
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:37,440
So you lost a companion?

234
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:39,540
We sure did.

235
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:43,960
The last time we saw her, she had collapsed not that far from the Mad Mage.

236
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,920
It's hard to be optimistic.

237
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:50,360
Still no excuse to lie to the rest of your party.

238
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:54,280
It's easy when it's not your problem, huh?

239
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:56,760
I was only kidding!

240
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:58,960
Behind you.

241
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:07,420
Just relax.

242
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:10,260
They're this town's residence.

243
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:16,540
The ghosts that reside in this area are still sane, and only appear when they want to be seen.

244
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:19,940
The paths that they travel are safe.

245
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,200
Let's follow.

246
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:26,580
Are you serious?

247
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:38,560
Down there.

248
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:40,540
That's where we were before.

249
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:42,840
But the red dragon is gone.

250
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:46,920
Did it come back to life, maybe?

251
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:47,680
No.

252
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:50,540
The dogs don't seem to be on high alert.

253
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:53,760
The mage either took it away, or made it disappear.

254
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:56,380
It looks like there was an explosion.

255
00:14:57,060 --> 00:15:00,280
A fire was lit near the dragon's fuel sack, and it exploded.

256
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:02,960
I'm shocked you survived.

257
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:06,900
One of our party members used abjuration magic and protected us.

258
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:08,600
So we were fine.

259
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:11,860
You roll with a pretty good party, don't you?

260
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,540
If you were there, you wouldn't be saying that.

261
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:17,980
The person who did it had no idea she could use that spell.

262
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:21,000
And later, our healer almost got us wiped out.

263
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:26,480
Sure, it eventually worked out in the end, but if it hadn't, we would have looked like real fools.

264
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,380
That's what I have to deal with.

265
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:37,260
By the way, how exactly did you all manage to defeat the red dragon?

266
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,020
Senshi and I distracted it.

267
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:46,980
And then the tall man, his name's Laios, by the way, jumped onto it and struck its weak point, which finally took the red dragon down.

268
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:48,460
That's pretty impressive.

269
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:52,260
Courageousness is a good quality for a fighter to have.

270
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:54,280
Oh, that wasn't courage.

271
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:59,000
It was fine since we succeeded, but it was a dumb gamble.

272
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:01,500
It really freaked me out.

273
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:04,280
How can these people live so recklessly like that?

274
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:08,200
We had two other party members who left our group.

275
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:14,460
Thinking about it now, seems like they were probably the smart ones.

276
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:18,660
I should have left then, but I guess I was too stubborn at the time.

277
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:24,280
So you're saying you would have been fine losing your remaining party?

